.TH SHITFETCH 7 "2026-05-26" "shitfetch 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
shitfetch \- overview, conventions, and notes
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shitfetch
is a small Linux fetch utility focused on straightforward local detection,
simple output, and an easy-to-hack C11 codebase.
.SH DESIGN NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Linux-only by design.
.IP \(bu 2
Configuration uses strict JSONC parsing.
.IP \(bu 2
Package counting is based on local package database state.
.IP \(bu 2
Language-specific package managers such as
.B npm
and
.B pip
are intentionally excluded.
.SH OUTPUT CONVENTIONS
The
.B packages
module emits a comma-separated list when several package stores are detected,
for example:
.PP
.RS
1234 (dpkg), 18 (flatpak)
.RE
.PP
System package managers are listed before universal stores such as
.B flatpak
and
.BR snap .
.SH PACKAGE MANAGER COVERAGE
The current file-based coverage includes:
.BR pacman ,
.BR dpkg ,
.BR apk ,
.BR xbps ,
.BR pkgtools ,
.BR scratchpkg ,
.BR paludis ,
.BR portage ,
.BR sorcery ,
.BR kiss ,
.BR opkg ,
.BR eopkg ,
.BR nix ,
.BR flatpak ,
.BR snap ,
and
.BR homebrew .
.PP
On Bedrock Linux,
.B shitfetch
aggregates package counts across supported strata-local databases.
